// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 08-alias-validity
// facility: [Compound-Assign] (D-0035, the hidden exclusive reference), [Read-Conflict], rule.control.frame-references (D-0284); conf.compound-call-target-reads-same-element-dynamic
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.aliasing-conflict (dynamic)
// expect-stdout-hex: 330a
//
// A target with a call is reached once, through a hidden exclusive
// reference that lives while the value is computed: `w[f()] += w[0]` is
// `{ auto t = &mut w[f()]; *t = *t + w[0]; }`. With two elements the read
// of `w[0]` is beside it; with one, `w[0]` is the element `t` holds, and
// the read conflicts. Which it is is a value: the run decides.

import std;

fn main()
{
    Vec<i32> w = Vec::filled(2, 1);
    w[Vec::len(&w) - 1] += w[0] + 1;
    printf("%v\n", w[1]);
    Vec<i32> u = Vec::filled(1, 1);
    u[Vec::len(&u) - 1] += u[0];
    printf("%v\n", u[0]);
}
